  "title": "(R)PROJ.------T.C.IMP.",
  "type": "crossing",
  "description": "Diagram in PCC-26. (R)PROJ — the reality of projection — is crossed with T-C-IMP (time continuum implications). PROJ → T-C-IMP (the crossing). Two lines branch from the main line. The first runs to TRS (transition); EXT-CON branches from TRS, and FUND-DYN (fundamental dynamics) and EXT-DYM (extended dynamics) branch from EXT-CON. The second runs to COS-P (cosmic particulars), which branches two ways: COS-P → IF-SPT (infra-spirituality) → RT-DY (reality dynamics) → PROG-CONT (progressional continuance), and COS-P → A-PR (all-purpose) → VT-DY (vibrational dynamics) → PHY-U-P (physical universe particular).",
